WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.707
What to take into the next lesson.

2
00:00:01.987 --> 00:00:05.592
Keyword search is an inverted index plus a ranking function.

3
00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:15.387
BM25 adds two ideas to TF-IDF: repeated mentions saturate (k1), and long documents are partly normalized (b).

4
00:00:15.667 --> 00:00:17.779
The defaults, k1 = 1.

5
00:00:18.059 --> 00:00:19.616
2 and b = 0.

6
00:00:19.896 --> 00:00:22.733
75, are good starting points, not truths.

7
00:00:23.013 --> 00:00:27.579
The tokenizer decides what can match at all, so test it with your identifiers.

8
00:00:27.859 --> 00:00:34.429
And keyword and embedding retrieval fail on different queries, which is a strong hint that combining them should help.

9
00:00:34.709 --> 00:00:41.067
The next lesson does that combination properly, because the obvious way to do it (add the scores) has a trap in it.
